# Frontend Rules

Stack: **Vanilla HTML/CSS/JS** — not React, Next.js, or Tailwind.

## Structure
- `index.html` — view shells only; prefer JS rendering for dynamic data
- `style.css` — design tokens and shared components
- `css/*.css` — feature styles (dx, perf, accessibility, visualizations, education)
- `js/api.js` — BlockchainAPI + ApiCache (all HTTP here)
- `js/ui.js` — UIRenderer dashboard
- Reuse: Hooks, UIStates, Toast, ErrorUtils, Accessibility, ModuleLoader

## Requirements
- Accessible: focus-visible, ARIA, keyboard support (see accessibility.js)
- Performant: ApiCache, Scheduler, skip DOM if fingerprint unchanged
- Lazy-load heavy modules (analytics, visualizations, education) via ModuleLoader
- JSDoc on new utility modules

## Do not
- Add a bundler or React without explicit request
- Duplicate API calls outside BlockchainAPI
- Use innerHTML without escaping user content (UIHelpers.escape)

## UI changes
- Match existing design tokens (--accent, --surface, etc.)
- Update DEVELOPER.md for new modules or config
- Update CHANGELOG.md for significant UX changes
